WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.229
Week 14: Travel, Transport, and Lodging. reserve transport and lodging check in report delays and room problems

2
00:00:08.229 --> 00:00:15.455
Cultural lens. Rail, bus, air, and shared transport practices; lodging types across regions.

3
00:00:15.455 --> 00:00:27.889
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.889 --> 00:00:39.896
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.896 --> 00:00:49.109
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:49.109 --> 00:01:20.807
Model language. El sistema ferroviario varía entre países. — The rail system varies between countries. Algunos viajeros prefieren la pensión al hotel. — Some travelers prefer a guesthouse to a hotel. Otros se quedan en un albergue. — Others stay in a hostel. El transporte compartido es común en varias regiones. — Shared transport is common in several regions. El vocabulario de viaje cambia según el país. — Travel vocabulary changes by country.

7
00:01:20.807 --> 00:01:30.961
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
